OVERVIEW: Forward DICOM events as HL7/FHIR messages (DICOM listener not
implemented)

Intended to receive DICOM instances and forward them as HL7 v2 or
FHIR messages.

Not implemented: the listener on --listen-port accepts TCP
connections but does not implement the PS3.8 DICOM Upper Layer
protocol or a Storage SCP (PS3.4 Annex B), so no DICOM
association can be made with it. Use the convert subcommands
(dicom-to-hl7, dicom-to-fhir) on files instead.

USAGE: dicom-gateway forward [--listen-port <listen-port>] [--forward-hl7 <forward-hl7>] [--forward-fhir <forward-fhir>] [--message-type <message-type>] [--verbose]

OPTIONS:
  --listen-port <listen-port>
                          TCP port to open (no PS3.8 Upper Layer / C-STORE SCP
                          is implemented) (default: 11112)
  --forward-hl7 <forward-hl7>
                          HL7 destination (e.g., hl7://server:2575)
  --forward-fhir <forward-fhir>
                          FHIR destination (e.g.,
                          https://fhir.example.com/ImagingStudy)
  --message-type <message-type>
                          HL7 message type to generate: ADT, ORM, ORU (default:
                          ORU)
  -v, --verbose           Verbose output
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

